  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the pricing code and project guidance, update `invoice.quote`, verify the edge cases, and record the design decision through the provided memory adapter.",
    "I’m applying the installed OpenSocrates guidance to the design decision and continuity record. Next I’ll compare the current helper contracts with the requested pricing rules.",
    "The existing `pricing.subtotal()` already enforces exact integer seat counts and nonnegative integer prices. `pricing.rules()` supplies the shipping values, so the change can stay in `invoice.quote` without duplicating validation or tariff constants.",
    "The pricing checks pass, including the 5,000 cent discount boundary, shipping after discount, zero priced international orders, invalid numeric inputs, the existing two argument call, and `app.total()`. I’ll save the bounded design decision and verify that the memory record was accepted.",
    "Updated [invoice.py](<disposable>/workspace/invoice.py) with optional `member=False`. Quotes now return integer subtotal, discount, shipping, and total amounts; apply the member discount to merchandise when the original subtotal qualifies; and use the discounted amount for domestic free shipping.\n\nPricing checks passed for the discount boundary, zero priced international orders, empty orders, invalid quantities and prices, the existing two argument call, and `app.total()`. The public design decision was recorded and confirmed as accepted in project memory."
  ],
